I am near the sea now.
I walk in a small lane near the sea.
There is an old sweets shop here.
I go into the shop.
The shop smells very nice.
I see fresh pedhas in a glass box.
These are special Maharashtrian pedhas.
I like these pedhas a lot.
I want to take these pedhas home.
I call the man in the shop.
"Dada, please give me one box," I say.
He packs a nice box for me.
"How much is this?" I ask him.
"Three hundred rupees, madam," he says.
I give him three hundred rupees.
He gives me the box of pedhas.
My work is now complete.
Today I make a long journey by bus and by metro.
But now I am very happy.
Now, I need to go back home.
